[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2763080571","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104754#issuecomment-2763080571","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104754","id":2763080571,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ksUN7","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-29T04:10:03Z","updated_at":"2025-03-30T10:59:16Z","body":"I'm not really a fan of the filename suffix approach, it's not very flexible. When I asked to add this TODO, I had another option in mind, directive comments, something like:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n# gdtest-enable-all-warnings\r\n# gdtest-disable-warnings: unused_variable, return_value_discarded\r\n```\r\n\r\nWith this approach, we could introduce as many test parameters as we need, instead of relying on suffixes.\r\n\r\nAlso, we could use the new `@warning_ignore_start` annotation to suppress uninteresting warnings at the file level. However, this would require changing a lot of files, so I'd rather we merge ~#100899~ #99899 first.\r\n\r\nFinally, the `UNTYPED_DECLARATION` and `INFERRED_DECLARATION` warnings work very well and are implemented with a small amount of code. The lack of ability to test them is not a big problem in my opinion, regressions are unlikely here.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2763080571/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2763084631","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104754#issuecomment-2763084631","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104754","id":2763084631,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ksVNX","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-29T04:22:15Z","updated_at":"2025-03-29T04:22:15Z","body":"I agree that the suffix approach isn't especially flexible. I wasn't sure if comments would be a good idea since they're technically a part of the GDScript text file itself, but I'm not sure exactly how those sorts of things are handled internally.\r\n\r\nAnother potential solution could be to include another (optional) file that lives alongside `some_test.gd`, like `some_test.warn`, which could override the default warning settings similarly to your comment example.\r\n\r\nLooking at the code that implements `UNTYPED_DECLARATION` and `INFERRED_DECLARATION`, it does look pretty simple. But as long as there isn't a big cost to having tests for the warnings, I think it'd be good to have them there just in case. It feels a bit strange to me to have tests for most of the warnings, but not these couple.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2763084631/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816416014","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104754#issuecomment-2816416014","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104754","id":2816416014,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6n3xkO","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-19T00:53:51Z","updated_at":"2025-04-19T00:53:51Z","body":"Given the inflexibility of this approach, and the fact that it's arguably not necessary to have tests for the static typing warnings anyways, I'll close this PR for now.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816416014/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]